<title>USA: San Francisco port OKs $260 mln ballpark plan.</title>
<headline>San Francisco port OKs $260 mln ballpark plan.</headline>
<dateline>SAN FRANCISCO 1997-07-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>San Francisco's port commission on Tuesday approved plans for building a $260 million waterfront ballpark for the Giants baseball team, city officials said.</p>
<p>The commission voted unanimously to support the team's long-term lease. The 25-year lease still must win over the San Francisco Board of Supervisors.</p>
<p>The funding package for Pacific Bell Park will include a $140 million syndicated bank financing and $100 million from naming rights, team officials said.</p>
<p>The Board of Supervisors' finance committee is scheduled to vote on the Giants' lease on Wednesday. If approved, the full board will consider the plan on July 28.</p>
<p>((-- San Francisco newsroom, 415-677-2511))</p>
